1. Create a new repository in your project directory.
2. Add the following code to the repository:
```php
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Broadcast;
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Model;

class MyRepository extends Model
{
    protected $table = 'my_table';
    protected $fillable = [
        'name', 'email', 'phone', 'date', 'created_at', 'updated_at'
    ];

    public function broadcasts()
    {
        return $this->belongsToMany(Broadcast::class);
    }

    public function broadcastsByName()
    {
        return $this->belongsToMany(Broadcast::class);
    }
}
```
3. Run the following command to commit the changes to the repository:
```php
php artisan migrate
```
4. Run the following command to create a new broadcast:
```php
php artisan make:broadcast --name=my_broadcast --phone=+1234567890
```
5. View the broadcasts in your application by navigating to `app/broadcasts/my_broadcast.json` and view the data.

